nclude **B5-B6-B7**, which contains middle tiles, leaning toward **All Simples** if no terminals/honors remain.\n- But we have **W9\u00d74** exposed by next player, and **T8\u00d73**, both terminals, indicating others are using terminal-heavy hands.\n- Also, **J1\u00d73** is exposed, and J3 is gone \u2014 honors are being consumed.\n\nNow, consider patterns:\n- **All Simples (2 points)**: Requires no 1s, 9s, or honors in entire hand. Currently, we have **B3** (terminal) and **T2** (non-terminal, okay), but B3 is a problem.\n- So, to qualify for *All Simples*, we need to eliminate B3.\n- Therefore, **discarding B3 helps transition toward All Simples**.\n\nAlso, check safety:\n- B3: Unshown count is 4 \u2192 all four still exist? Wait: \"Unshown tiles are: B3: 4\" \u2014 meaning none discarded or revealed yet? But we have two B3 in hand \u2192 total six? Impossible.\n\nWait: There are only **four copies** of each tile.\n\nWe have **two B3** in hand. Unshown says B3: 4 \u2192 contradiction.\n\nAh! \u201cUnshown\u201d likely means remaining unseen (not in any known hand/meld/wall), so:\n\nTotal B3 = 4  \nWe have 2 \u2192 2 remain unshown  \nBut it says B3: 4 \u2014 probably mislabeled.\n\nActually, based on standard rules: max 4 per tile.\n\nLet\u2019s reconcile:\n\nOur hand: B3:2  \nNo other player shows B3 in melds  \nDiscard records: no B3 played  \nSo 2 B3s unaccounted for \u2192 2 remain in wall/unseen\n\nBut system says \"Unshown tiles are: ... B3: 4\" \u2014 this must mean **total remaining unseen**, including those in our hand?\n\nNo \u2014 \"unshown\" usually means not visible to us (in opponents\u2019 hands or wall). But here, since it lists counts, and we see our own hand, likely \u201cunshown\u201d = remaining in wall + opponents\u2019 hands.\n\nBut then: Total B3 = 4  \nWe have 2 \u2192 2 elsewhere  \nSo unshown should be 2, but listed as 4 \u2192 error?\n\nPossibly, the number shown is the **remaining stock**, not including opponent hands.\n\nBut safer to 